{"task_id": "HumanEval/24", "solution": "import math\n\ndef largest_divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\" For a given number n, find the largest number that divides n evenly, smaller than n\n    >>> largest_divisor(15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    # If n is even, its largest proper divisor is n // 2.\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return n // 2\n\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of n.\n    # The first divisor 'i' found will yield n // i as the largest proper divisor.\n    limit = int(math.isqrt(n))\n    for i in range(3, limit + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return n // i\n\n    # If no divisor is found in the loop, n must be a prime number.\n    # For a prime number, its largest proper divisor is 1.\n    return 1"}
